stateDiagram-v2
  state "Cancel unstarted tick" as CancelUnstarted
  state "Drain committed capture" as DrainCommitted
  state "Await owned child exit" as AwaitExit
  state "Normal worker stop" as NormalStop
  state "Resolve owned holder" as ResolveHolder
  [*] --> Running: owned worker ready
  Running --> Closed: normal end / suppress future ticks
  Running --> Failed: failure, signal or unexpected exit
  Closed --> CancelUnstarted: sleeping or pending tick
  Closed --> DrainCommitted: capture already committed
  CancelUnstarted --> AwaitExit: sleep finishes and matched stop ack
  DrainCommitted --> AwaitExit: clean qualification and matched stop ack
  DrainCommitted --> Failed: interrupted, unavailable or expired
  AwaitExit --> NormalStop: exact child exit zero AND published reap
  AwaitExit --> Failed: missing ack, wrong child, nonzero, signal or missing record
  CancelUnstarted --> Failed: sleep failure or missing record
  NormalStop --> Collection: same owner and writer domain
  Failed --> ResolveHolder: preserve first failure and all partials
  ResolveHolder --> Collection: holder resolved for collection only
  ResolveHolder --> Unresolved: unknown holder or containment expiry
  Collection --> [*]: independent audit and exact-stop outcomes retained
  Unresolved --> [*]: no acceptance or later slot
  note right of CancelUnstarted
    No capture attempt ordinal.
    Normal stop sends no signal.
  end note
  note right of NormalStop
    Requires clean prior history.
    Never clears an earlier failure.
  end note
  note left of DrainCommitted
    Uses original operation deadline.
    Numerical profile remains design work.
  end note
